493626","violation_type_title":"Training Requirements for Employees, Caregivers, and Directors - 24 Annual training (26 TAC §746.1301(a)(5)(A))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20241212-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1605-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20241212","date":"2024-12-12","original_code":"746.1605(1)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-12-16","finding":"Child/Caregiver Ratio - 18 Months Difference in Age: Three older infants were grouped with an older group of children with the oldest child five years of age. The age gap between the youngest infant and the oldest child exceed 18 months.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026373886","violation_type_title":"Child/Caregiver Ratio - 18 Months Difference in Age (26 TAC §746.1605(1))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20241212-v6","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2431","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20241212","date":"2024-12-12","original_code":"746.2431","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-12-16","finding":"Infant Daily Report - Share with Parent: Daily sheets have not been routinely completed for infants 12-17 months of age. It was confirmed at inspection that daily sheets were not being shared through the bright wheel app with parents once the infants turned 12 months of age.","topic":"records","source_record_id":"1026453791","violation_type_title":"Infant Daily Report - Share with Parent (26 TAC §746.2431)","topic_label":"Records, permits & program"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20241212-v7","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1205-a-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20241212","date":"2024-12-12","original_code":"746.1205(a)(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-12-16","finding":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity: A child  in care was left alone with an adult that is not a caregiver employed with the operation.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026533988","violation_type_title":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity (26 TAC §746.1205(a)(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20241212-v8","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-5205-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20241212","date":"2024-12-12","original_code":"746.5205(1)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-12-16","finding":"Fire Drill Monthly - Exit in 3 Minutes: The last two months of fire drills were not able to be completed in three minutes or less. One drill took 3 minutes and 15 seconds and one took 4 minutes to be able to exit.","topic":"fire","source_record_id":"1026293069","violation_type_title":"Fire Drill Monthly - Exit in 3 Minutes (26 TAC §746.5205(1))","topic_label":"Fire safety & emergency drills"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20241212-v9","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-901-5","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20241212","date":"2024-12-12","original_code":"746.901(5)","severity":"medium_low","severity_label":"Medium-low risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-12-16","finding":"Required Personnel Records - Required Affidavit (Form 2912): One staff personnel files lack form 2912 pre employment affidavit for staff that were hired after September 2023.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026293068","violation_type_title":"Required Personnel Records - Required Affidavit (Form 2912) (26 TAC §746.901(5))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20241212-v10","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-305-a-7","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20241212","date":"2024-12-12","original_code":"746.305(a)(7)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Corrected at inspection","finding":"Report Change in Controlling Person: An individual listed on the controlling person list is past due for being removed. This was put into compliance with having the director put in writing that this individual can be removed from the controlling person list by child care regulation.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026293067","violation_type_title":"Report Change in Controlling Person (26 TAC §746.305(a)(7))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20240702","date":"2024-07-02","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905855683","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905855683","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2024-07-02","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20240627","date":"2024-06-27","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":4,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905855682","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905855682","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2024-06-27","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20240627-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1205-a-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20240627","date":"2024-06-27","original_code":"746.1205(a)(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-07-02","finding":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity: The sole infant caregiver was observed leaving the classroom to complete tasks in the kitchen on two different occasions during the inspection. The caregiver did not have auditory and visual awareness of the infants and was not within physical proximity. Additionally, the sole pre k caregiver additional left the classroom to complete other tasks.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026514564","violation_type_title":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity (26 TAC §746.1205(a)(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20240627-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2505-4-c","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20240627","date":"2024-06-27","original_code":"746.2505(4)(C)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-07-02","finding":"Furnishings and Equipment for Toddlers - Never Allow Toddlers to Sleep or Walk With Bottles and Training Cups: Toddlers were observed walking around while drinking their sippy cups. The caregiver did not attempt to redirect them to sit while drinking their sippy cups.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026434285","violation_type_title":"Furnishings and Equipment for Toddlers - Never Allow Toddlers to Sleep or Walk With Bottles and Training Cups (26 TAC §746.2505(4)(C))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20240627-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3317","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20240627","date":"2024-06-27","original_code":"746.3317","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-07-02","finding":"Food Service and Preparation Requirement - Safe and Sanitary: The toddler snack items were observed being stored on the lid of the classroom trash can that is used to store dirty diapers in preparation for snack time.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026434284","violation_type_title":"Food Service and Preparation Requirement - Safe and Sanitary (26 TAC §746.3317)","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20240627-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2201","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20240627","date":"2024-06-27","original_code":"746.2201","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-07-02","finding":"Planned Activities Designed to Meet Individual Needs: The morning drop off room is used for 90 minutes with the pre k age classroom with the only available activity of large duplo blocks. Alternative activities were not offered by the staff. For the first 30 minutes of the morning, the group is mixed with infants and toddlers as well. Additional planned activities are needed to ensure the individual needs of each age group have variety of choices to engage in during morning activities.","topic":"facilities","source_record_id":"1026514565","violation_type_title":"Planned Activities Designed to Meet Individual Needs (26 TAC §746.2201)","topic_label":"Facilities & equipment"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20240620","date":"2024-06-20","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":7,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905855681","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905855681","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2024-06-20","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20240620-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-603-a-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20240620","date":"2024-06-20","original_code":"746.603(a)(4)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-07-08","finding":"Children's Records - Immunizations: Two children's records was lacking immunization records.","topic":"health","source_record_id":"1026258501","violation_type_title":"Children's Records - Immunizations (26 TAC §746.603(a)(4))","topic_label":"Health records & medication"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20240620-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3417-3","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20240620","date":"2024-06-20","original_code":"746.3417(3)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-06-27","finding":"Children Handwashing After Toileting or Diapering: The sink in the infant classroom is not working and the children were unable to have their hands washed at the hand washing sink after diaper changing, before meal times and after outdoor activities.","topic":"sanitation","source_record_id":"1026379462","violation_type_title":"Children Handwashing After Toileting or Diapering (26 TAC §746.3417(3))","topic_label":"Sanitation & hygiene"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20240620-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1205-a-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20240620","date":"2024-06-20","original_code":"746.1205(a)(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-06-27","finding":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity: Staff were observed at inspection leaving their classrooms unsupervised for other job-related tasks on seven different occurrences during the duration of the inspection.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026339111","violation_type_title":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity (26 TAC §746.1205(a)(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20240620-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3415-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20240620","date":"2024-06-20","original_code":"746.3415(4)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-06-27","finding":"Employee Handwashing After Diapering a Child: The sink in the infant classroom is not working and the caregiver failed to do appropriate hand washing after diaper changing.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026459315","violation_type_title":"Employee Handwashing After Diapering a Child (26 TAC §746.3415(4))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20240620-v5","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1301-a-4-a","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20240620","date":"2024-06-20","original_code":"746.1301(a)(4)(A)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-06-28","finding":"Training Requirements for Employees, Caregivers, and Directors - Pediatric CPR: A caregiver was re-hired and the CPR training for her expired in January 2024. The caregiver was observed at inspection supervising a classroom as the only caregiver in that classroom without CPR training.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026419382","violation_type_title":"Training Requirements for Employees, Caregivers, and Directors - Pediatric CPR (26 TAC §746.1301(a)(4)(A))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20240620-v6","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-4751-d","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1392476-i20240620","date":"2024-06-20","original_code":"746.4751(d)","severity":"medium","severity_label":"Medium risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-06-27","finding":"Maintenance Procedures for Active Play - Keep Records for 3 Months: Documentation of monthly checks of the active play space was not available at inspection.","topic":"safety","sou